<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 0.9em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 1st Grade (CEFR: Pre-A1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Colors in Our World</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> It's an Orange Cat.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Identify the topic of a conversation that involves familiar subjects. Interactive: Respond to simple conversations on familiar topics by using gestures or by pointing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can show comprehension of age-appropriate numbers when paired with familiar objects (e.g., identifying "three blue flowers" by pointing to the correct group). Can identify colors and objects when spoken about (e.g., "blue bird" or "red flower"). Can follow simple instructions related to colors and familiar objects by pointing or gesturing (e.g., "Find the blue bird.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 47%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students with a "Hello Song" using simple gestures. The teacher holds up a large, colorful picture flashcard of a cat and asks, "What is it?" (Teacher prompts "Cat!"). The teacher then shows an orange object (e.g., an orange ball, a flashcard of an orange fruit) and says "Orange."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a flashcard of an orange cat and clearly states, "It is an orange cat." The teacher repeats the phrase slowly, pointing to the cat and then the color. The teacher models the initial sound /k/ in "cat" and the /l/ sound in "blue" using flashcards for "blue bird" and "green leaf" while saying the words slowly and clearly for students to hear and imitate chorally.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher uses TPR and visuals to check understanding.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Holding up the orange cat flashcard) "Is it a dog?" (Students shake heads "No.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Holding up a blue bird flashcard) "Is it red?" (Students shake heads "No."). "What color is it?" (Teacher prompts "Blue!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Show me the cat." (Students point to the cat flashcard).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Colors in Our World")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A large, colorful poster depicting a simple outdoor scene with a tree, a house, the sky, a cat, a bird, and flowers. Alternatively, a short audio recording (teacher-recorded or simple song/chant) describing the scene.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Recognizing colors and objects: Identify familiar objects by color (e.g., "blue bird" or "red flower.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher shows the poster/plays the audio.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Look! See the sky. It is blue. See a bird. It is a blue bird. See the cat. It is an orange cat. Look! A red flower. A green leaf on the tree." (Teacher uses a pointer to highlight objects as they are named).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Listening focus):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist:</b> "Are we talking about animals or colors?" (Teacher shows flashcards for 'animals' and 'colors'. Students point to 'colors').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Point and Identify (TPR):</b> "Point to the blue bird." "Show me the orange cat." "Where is the red flower?" "Point to the green leaf." (Teacher repeats for several objects and colors, encouraging quick pointing responses).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Color + noun (e.g., "blue bird"), Present simple (e.g., "It is an orange cat.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> cat, bird, flower, leaf, tree, house, sky, blue, orange, red, green, tall, fly, sit, grow.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> /l/ in "blue" and "leaf"; initial sounds /b/ in "bird," /k/ in "cat," /f/ in "flower."</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: "Listen and Point to the Color-Object Pair"</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher places flashcards of different colored objects (e.g., an orange cat, a blue bird, a red flower, a green leaf, a tall tree) on the board or floor. The teacher says a phrase like, "Point to the red flower." Students listen and point to the correct flashcard. The teacher repeats with other combinations, including attention to initial sounds: "Listen: /b/ /b/ bird. Point to the BLUE bird." "Listen: /l/ /l/ leaf. Point to the GREEN leaf."</p></li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: "Listen and Circle/Color"</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students receive a worksheet with outline drawings of objects (e.g., a cat, a bird, a flower, a leaf, a house). The teacher gives instructions: "Listen carefully. Color the cat orange." "Color the bird blue." "Color one flower red." "Color the leaf green." "Draw two blue flowers." (Students follow listening instructions by coloring/drawing on their worksheets). The teacher circulates, observing and providing support.</p></li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Interactive Practice: "Listen and Do (TPR Story)"</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher tells a very short, simple story using the target vocabulary and actions, and students respond with TPR. "The orange cat sits. (Students pretend to sit). The blue bird flies. (Students flap arms). The red flower grows. (Students slowly raise hands). The tall tree grows. (Students stand tall). See the green leaf on the tree." The teacher repeats the story, allowing students to practice listening and responding with actions.</p></li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>15-17 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Colors in Our World")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task:</b> "Listen and Create My Colorful World."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students receive a blank paper or a simple outline drawing of a basic landscape (e.g., a line for ground, an empty sky area, an outline of a house and a tree). The teacher gives a series of simple, sequenced instructions. Students listen and draw/color on their paper according to the instructions. This task requires active listening and comprehension of colors, objects, and simple quantities.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "First, draw a big, green tree."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Next, draw one orange cat sitting under the tree."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Then, draw two red flowers near the house."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Now, draw a blue bird flying in the blue sky."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Draw three green leaves on the tree."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher repeats instructions slowly and clearly, giving students time to listen and execute each step before moving to the next. The focus is on students' ability to listen and follow the multi-element instructions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during "Listen and Create My Colorful World" task (Stage 4) and review of students' completed drawings.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' completed drawings from Stage 4 (their "Colorful World" picture).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher checklist):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can identify colors and objects when spoken about (e.g., drew a "red flower").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can follow simple instructions related to colors and familiar objects by drawing/pointing (e.g., drew the "orange cat" in the correct place).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Shows comprehension of age-appropriate numbers when paired with familiar objects (e.g., drew "two red flowers" or "three green leaves").</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher shows a picture of a happy face and a sad face.) "I can hear the color 'red'." (Students point to the happy or sad face).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can hear the word 'bird'." (Students point to the happy or sad face).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new colors did you hear today?" (Students can point to colored objects in the classroom or flashcards).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is your favorite animal color?" (Teacher prompts: "Red flower?" "Blue bird?" and students point).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in engaging students and developing their listening skills for colors and objects? (e.g., TPR, flashcards, specific instructions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson, especially regarding vocabulary retention or comprehension of multi-step instructions for Pre-A1.3 learners? (e.g., more repetition, slower pace, simpler instructions).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> "Today we listened to many colors and objects like a 'blue bird' and an 'orange cat'. Next time, we will look at a picture story about these colorful friends and listen for their names and colors as we read."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1<br>3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>